A space group is a mathematical representation of the symmetry of a crystal structure. It is a mathematical group that describes the symmetry operations that can be applied to the unit cell of a crystal and leave the crystal to be identical. These symmetry operations include rotations, translations, and reflections. The space group is determined by the symmetry of the unit cell and the space it repeats in the crystal lattice. 

In crystallography, the space group is fundamental for understanding the crystal structure and its properties. It is used to determine the crystal structure, calculate the crystal constants, and predict the physical properties of the crystal. 

\boxed{\text{The symmetry group is a mathematical representation of the symmetry operations that can be applied to the unit cell of a crystal and leave the crystal to be identical.}}

